    "explanation": "This was a verified rider no-show. The $5.00 cancellation fee you contested, rider, stands as it is, and the driver is paid $4.00.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver accepted at 07:43:53 and the platform's own GPS auto-arrival recorded him within 10 m of the Woodlands Interchange PHV bay at 07:53:00 at 0 km/h, with the 300-second free waiting period starting at 07:53:02. His exported GPS trace shows one continuous qualifying stationary run inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius of 556 seconds (07:53:00 to 08:02:16, 57 qualifying fixes) — comfortably past the 300-second minimum dwell — and he cancelled at 08:02:20 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, 560 seconds after the first in-geofence fix and so clear of the 480-second no-show threshold carried on this trip. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold: (a) the arrived event is present; (b) the trace places him inside the geofence at that timestamp; (c) the dwell exceeds the free waiting period and the cancellation falls after the longer threshold; (d) no boarding event, driver-terminated with a recognised no-show code after the dwell elapsed. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 — he was at the bay and stationary, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h — so the waiting clock runs as recorded and no recomputation shortens the dwell. Nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee.\n\nYour own evidence, rider, does not support your claim that you were still inside the interchange. Your rider track carries 90 fixes from 07:50:40 to 08:04:00 at a mean distance of about 800 m from the pickup pin (minimum 796.46 m, maximum 804.18 m) with zero qualifying fixes inside the 200 m rider-presence radius. POL-NS-04 limb (c) is therefore affirmatively failed on admissible fixes and the clause cannot exonerate you; POL-NS-11 does not apply because the track exists and the test could be run. The driver's 07:53:25 message 'hi im at the bay, where are you' and your 'coming' at 07:55:20 change nothing — he had already served the full waiting period and cancelled well after it.\n\nThe surviving claims on both sides agree on the material points and I accept them: the platform-confirmed arrival (POL-NS-12), the 556-second dwell, the 560 seconds to cancellation past the 480-second threshold, the RIDER_NO_SHOW code, the reconciliation of the $5.00 fare line with the $5.00 platform figure in force (no POL-NS-08(d) defect), and the profile arithmetic. On the last point, POL-NS-07 withholds compensation only where no_show_terminations_30d is 4 or more AND the ratio to completed_trips_30d exceeds 0.08; the driver's figures are 1 and 1/112 ≈ 0.009, so neither limb holds.\n\nIntegrity and escalation. No POL-NS-08 limb (a)–(d) impairment exists: the arrival event sits on a trace fix (no clock skew), the trace has 100% coverage with a 0.0 s maximum gap, the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 2 with intact sequence numbering, and the fare line reconciles. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below 3), both profiles show 0 disputes_with_counterparty_90d, the anti-farming check is not tripped, and the artifacts do not conflict. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02703-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, but the dwell was a single uninterrupted run, so no accumulation is needed and no surviving claim rests on it; three claims that cited that artifact without naming its issue code were discarded at the citation check and are recorded below.\n\nOutcome. Under POL-NS-07 the driver receives 80% of the $5.00 fee in force = $4.00, the platform retaining $1.00 (the 20% service fee); the charge itself remains in place. Per POL-GEN-03 the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same $4.00 figure as driver_compensation_sgd. The monetary effect is $4.00, below the $8.00 execution threshold of POL-GEN-05, so it executes on issue. Confidence is 0.90, capped at 1.00 because every artifact carrying a deciding fact — trip record, GPS trace, fare ledger and driver profile — sits at weight 1.00, with the trip record's platform telemetry an independent carrier from the exported trace under POL-NS-12. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
