    "explanation": "To both parties: the $5.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on this trip stands, and the driver is paid $4.00 of it out of that fee. Here is why.\n\nFOR THE DRIVER. Every limb of POL-NS-01 holds on this record. (a) The trip record EV-TRIP-02703 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 07:53:00. (b) The exported trace EV-GPS-02703 places the driver's first qualifying fix inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius at 07:53:00, within 10 m of the pin at 0 km/h. (c) He then held position for a continuous 556 seconds (07:53:00 to 08:02:16, 57 qualifying fixes). That exceeds the 300-second free waiting period in force (platform_policy.free_wait_sec) and also clears the 480-second no-show threshold (platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec): measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix — not from the arrival tap — that threshold fell due at 08:01:00, and the driver cancelled at 08:02:20. (d) No boarding event is recorded and the trip was terminated by the driver under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises, at 08:02:20, after the dwell had elapsed. The arrival marker is not a false one under POL-NS-05: the driver was stationary at 0 km/h at the marker, not more than 300 m away and not moving at 15 km/h or above, so no recomputation shortens the clock. POL-NS-06 does not displace the fee either — there is no shortfall to refund, because 556 seconds is longer than the 300-second minimum — and POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue.\n\nFOR THE RIDER. I cannot accept that you were still inside the interchange when the driver cancelled. Your own device track in EV-GPS-02703 runs from 07:50:40 to 08:04:00 at a mean distance of 800.5 m from the pickup pin (minimum 796.5 m), with zero qualifying fixes inside the 200 m TRANSPORT_HUB rider-presence radius. Your message 'coming' at 07:55:20 confirms you had not reached the bay. POL-NS-04 therefore cannot exonerate you: its limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes, and the clause does not apply. The rider-presence test was runnable, so this is not a POL-NS-11 undecidable case.\n\nMONEY. With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the $5.00 cancellation fee in force — $4.00 — with the residual 20 percent retained as the platform service fee. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 112 is about 0.009 (below 0.08), and both limbs must hold. The fare ledger EV-FARE-02703 reconciles: its $5.00 cancellation-fee line matches platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of $5.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect.\n\nEVIDENCE INTEGRITY. The trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown all carry admissibility status COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, with 100 percent trace coverage, no gaps and a 10-second cadence; the fare reconciles and the chat sequence is intact, so no POL-NS-08 limb (a) to (d) is engaged and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires. The only impaired artifact is the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02703-01, weight 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT: it can carry no fact and nothing in this ruling rests on it, so it does not affect the outcome.\n\nThe monetary effect is $4.00, which is at or below the $8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so this provisional ruling is executed automatically on issue, subject to the POL-GEN-04 appeal route. No clause of the policy produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty."
